  "date": "2026-08-21",
  "purpose": "Systematically map, across models (135M/360M/1.5B), contexts (2048-32768, one pressure point at 200000-equivalent scale), and CPU/GPU KV split ratios, whether ANY tested regime shows KV placement as a real performance bottleneck (>=10% slowdown, predeclared threshold) -- to decide whether further investment in dynamic tiering scheduler sophistication (Phase 12F) is justified, or whether the demonstrated value of the Phase 12B-12E mechanism is elsewhere.",
  "literal_verdict": "KV_PLACEMENT_CAPACITY_ONLY_ON_TESTED_REGIME",
  "verdict_summary": "Across 16 benchmark batches spanning 135M/360M/1.5B models, contexts from 2048 to 32768, Q8_0 and Q5_1, and CPU/GPU KV split ratios from 0% to 100% GPU-resident, zero tested points cleared the predeclared >=10% slowdown threshold for a MEANINGFUL/STRONG bottleneck classification -- every point classified NO_BOTTLENECK. The single worst-case point across the entire sweep (1.5B, ctx=8192, 50% GPU-KV) was actually a 0.51% SPEEDUP relative to 100%-GPU-KV, not a slowdown. Pareto analysis at 135M/ctx=2048 shows the 0%-GPU-KV (all-CPU) point as the Pareto-optimal one (lowest VRAM, highest tok/s) among the tested ratios. CPU-resident KV was therefore at parity or faster than GPU-resident KV at every valid tested point -- the demonstrated product value of KV placement in this tested regime is VRAM capacity (freeing headroom for larger context), not throughput. A performance-driven dynamic policy was explicitly stopped based on this data.",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/kv-placement-bottleneck/summary.json:decision_gate (literal source field, one of five predeclared allowed enum values; not synthesized)",
  "productized": true,
  "product_pr": 21,
  "product_commit": "8287e8c14f1b5af2e9e17fa95e85663e94697d85",
  "productization_note": "This phase's capacity-only finding, together with Phase 12B's minimal device-override mechanism, is the direct research input to PR #21's static `--kv-placement` planner. PR #21's own description cites this phase's literal verdict string (KV_PLACEMENT_CAPACITY_ONLY_ON_TESTED_REGIME) and its own measured central result (a real Vulkan OOM at ctx=28500 with default placement, avoided by `auto`/`cpu`, a ~6.4% measured context uplift at that ONE configuration, explicitly disclosed as narrow) is consistent with -- but is the product team's OWN separate measurement, not a copy of this phase's sweep data. No code from this phase's tools/membrane-kv-bottleneck-analysis/ exists on product main (verified via git grep) -- only the FINDING was productized, not the analysis code itself.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "NVIDIA GTX 1650 (4096 MiB VRAM), Vulkan backend",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-135M-Instruct",
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct",
    "qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-fp16"
  ],
